==Evolution==
Evolves into '''The Death Moon''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''The Chaos Moon''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Ultra Kaguya''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]] and Behemoth Stones.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like the other [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]], Princess Kaguya has significantly different stats between Normal/Ultra Form (spammable) and Evolved/True Form (high performance), both of which can be used effectively depending on the situation.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Use Kaguya to stall Metal and Angel enemies within her range. She is beyond effective against stages like [[Utopia is Over There]]. Her strength comes from being extremely cost-efficient and hitting very often, to the point that she can't even be rushed down by a [[Doge Dark]], who would instead be juggled back continuously. However, she lacks in defense, range and offense otherwise, relying on only trait-compatible slow to keep her safe, meaning she can still be reached and wiped out by enemies who can withstand her relatively weak attacks or have greater range. This is less of a problem with recurring Metals as they often have even less range, but she can't always work against Angels, which have several backliners and midrangers like [[Angelic Sleipnir]], [[Sunfish Jones]] and [[Chickful A]].

==='''Evolved Form'''===
The Death Moon's chance to [[Slow]] is generally not enough to be of much use in most situations, so, as long as you are dealing with enemies that can be outranged by Princess Kaguya, you should use her Normal Form. As a high-performance unit, who isn't as replaceable, The Death Moon should be protected by many meatshields. As a frail backliner with long attack windup, she is best suited for non-aggressive approaches with many meatshields or tanks, so it may stay safe in the backlines and land hits often.

==='''True Form'''===
Due to her increased range, The Chaos Moon can now target enemies like [[Master A.]] and [[THE SLOTH]] more safely. Furthermore, her improved ability of a guaranteed slow now makes her a much more consistent crowd-controller, now able to, sometimes, outperform her Normal Form against even short-ranged targets.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
Kaguya goes back to her first form's low cost and spammable cooldown, though she also goes back to the stats and slow ability of that form (besides health, which is improved). The main buff here, however, is Metal Killer, which adds a GUARANTEED chance to take off 12% of a Metal enemy's current health on every hit. With this ability, [[Metal Cyclone]] and [[Sir Metal Seal]] can quickly lose most of their health to Ultra Kaguya's rapid Area Attacks with no need to rely on any luck. Considering that this form costs a mere 600¢ and can fully recharge in only 7.2 seconds, these powerful attacks are spammable. This alone would make the Ultra Form a sound investment to anyone who has the resources and struggles with Metals or Single Target attacks.

Against angels, she discovers a newfound potential as a [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]] sidegrade: exchanging attack rate, recharge time, and slow duration for increased survivability, better damage, and more range. This makes her especially useful for mixed stages, where she can put a noticeable dent in annoying peons while also slowing her target traits simultaneously. Additionally, her range advantage over Sanzo guarantees her survivability in scenarios where he would have faltered; her ridiculously high health allows her to reposition at least once, which is a privilege that Sanzo is ordinarily not privy to without ungodly amounts of boosting. Overall, where Sanzo fails to find utility outside of the traits he targets, Ultra Kaguya can shine in situations where he acts as nothing more than a hole in your wallet.

==='''Talents'''===
Remember that Kaguya's Talent from her True Form carry over to her Ultra Form!

The first Talent you should unlock is most likely '''Defense Buff''', as she will need every bit of health she can get in case an enemy reaches her, this is especially true in her Ultra Form where it could allow her the opportunity to reposition one more time. Though, it is more effective to use your [[Catseye]]s first. '''Slow''' is also quite useful, seeing that she can delay an Angel or two for a bit longer, but it's only a second more at max, so beware. '''Attack Buff''' can also help, but at most it's just extra chip damage for peons and angels, Metals won't even be affected anyway. '''Resist Slow''' is, with all Resist Talents, situational and most likely not worth it. '''Knockback''' is counterproductive, as it can make hard-hitters miss, and will also likely cause any stack of Ultra Kaguyas you build up to instantly knock away Metals before they can even kill them.

In short, Kaguya's Talents aren't the flashiest, but they can give a helping hand to her stats.

==='''Orb'''===
Defense up is the only effect orb with any use; it is useful for the same reasons as her defense up talent.

As for ability orbs, Death Mini-Surge is a double-edged sword: it can shred Metals with her Metal Killer, but it will also slow these enemies when they are behind the frontlines and potentially cause problems. Cash Back could be useful, but Kaguya is relatively cheap anyway. Resist Knockback won't be much help, and Stories of Legend Buff is completely useless. Colossus Slayer won't do much as she isn't much use against Colossus enemies anyway. Resist Wave can potentially be useful against enemies like [[Koronium]].

