==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Princess Kaguya was a part of three other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Sun and Moon (Removed Combo)|Sun and Moon]], [[Ancient Heroes (Removed Combo)|Ancient Heroes]] and [[Ultra Souls (Removed Combo)|Ultra Souls]].
*In [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]], Ultra Kaguyas that attacked the same target at once would all do the same amount of damage rather than doing less for each hit, making it possible to kill Metal enemies instantly by stacking and syncing nine Ultra Kaguyas to do 108% damage in a single frame. This was patched out in Version 13.3.1.
*There was a grammar mistake in The Chaos Moon's description. It was supposed to say "That can happen", but instead it said "That can happens". This was fixed in [[Version 15.1 Update|Version 15.1]].
*Ultra Kaguya is the first unit to have the Metal Killer ability.
*Princess Kaguya is based on the traditional Japanese legend ''[[wikipedia:The Tale of the Bamboo Cutter|The Tale of the Bamboo Cutter]]'', also known as ''The Tale of Princess Kaguya''. She originated from a bamboo shoot and was found by a bamboo cutter that was taking down the plant.
**In some iterations of the legend, Princess Kaguya was actually sent from the Moon and ultimately returns, hence the Moon-themed superweapons and the mention of her return in Ultra Kaguya's Japanese description.
**The Evolved and True Forms keep the reference to Kaguya's folktale through the attack, which causes bamboo to sprout.
*The rabbits next to the Evolved and True Forms may be based on various myths of a [[wikipedia:Moon rabbit|Moon rabbit]].
*This is actually the second Princess Kaguya in the series. The [[Media:Kumanchu enemy guide 17.png|first]] appeared as the boss of the [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]] in [[Kumanchu Royale]], with a different design and a [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] sister named [[Media:Kumanchu enemy guide 19.png|Shu KAGUYA]] (朱・KAGUYA, "Vermilion KAGUYA").
**The one in Kumanchu Royale was named カグヤ姫, while the one in [[The Battle Cats]] is かぐやひめ. These are different spellings of ''Kaguya-hime'' and directly translate to "Princess Kaguya".
*The Death Moon and The Chaos Moon closely resemble the [[wikia:starwars:Death Star|Death Star]], a superweapon from the ''Star Wars'' franchise.

